nodecode-ms-decision is a rewrite of guglxni's guglxni/ms-decision-provider:

  https://github.com/guglxni/ms-decision-provider
  commit a28887362a55f9b4b03362568760ce6d0ae903e5
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Aaryan Guglani (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: provider.py's Microsoft-Decision-1 client is carried into
Common Lisp. The one POST to {base}/providers/microsoft/v1/systemone, its
three typed question shapes (noul, choice, score), the batched decide call,
the api-key header, the deployment default ms-decision-1, the environment
names AZURE_FOUNDRY_API_KEY and AZURE_FOUNDRY_BASE_URL, the endpoint check
that accepts only an https <resource>.openai.azure.com host and strips a
/resource path or a trailing slash, the sanitized HTTP error that never echoes
the body, and the rule that nothing is sent until both the endpoint and the
key are set all keep their behaviour. The four registered tools keep their
names (decision_noul, decision_choice, decision_score, decide) and answer
the endpoint's JSON with the whole probability distribution, as the plugin
did. The optional pre_tool_call gate is carried onto the :TOOL point: the
same idea (only a fixed tool label and allowlisted operation words leave the
machine, never arguments), the same fixed risk set reduced to Nodecode's own
tool names, the same approve and block modes and block threshold, with the
operator asked through Nodecode's own question board instead of Hermes's
approval prompt.

What was left out, and why: Hermes's plugin context (register(ctx), the tool
and hook registries) is replaced by the cell declaration, so there is no
plugin.yaml or __init__.py. The per-process HMAC rule_key that let Hermes
cache an approval for one exact call has no counterpart here: Nodecode asks
per call and keeps no approval rule on disk, so the key and the cache are
gone. The shadow replay harness under tests/ (replay.py, decision_cases.json
and its metrics) is not carried; the cell's own offline tests stand in its
place. The plugin's secret-scope reader (agent.secret_scope.get_secret) is
replaced by the shared auth.json entry api_keys.ms-decision and the
environment variable, which is how a Nodecode cell reaches a key.
